course: dictionary
lesson: 4467
title: A bean with a French name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A haricot is a noun, so it names a thing: a haricot is a small white bean. You will also see «haricot bean», which means the same thing said in full. The example «Baked beans are usually haricot beans, which first came from the Americas» tells you what the word names, so use the sentence to check your meaning.
explain: Haricot is a French word, the French word for bean. That is a clue to look for. When you see a French word in a recipe, like «haricots verts», the words around it help you work out the meaning, and a dictionary settles it.
explain: Say it «HA-ri-koh», with the t silent. In the UK, Ireland and Australia, tinned baked beans in tomato sauce are haricot beans, but in the US the same bean is called a navy bean. Different places, different names, same bean.
fact: A haricot is a small white bean.
fact: Haricot beans are the kind used to make baked beans.
fact: «Haricot» is the French word for bean.
fact: «Haricots verts» means thin green beans in French cooking.
fact: Beans are seeds and are a good source of protein and fibre.
exercise: «Baked beans are usually haricot beans, which first came from the Americas.» What is a haricot? | A kind of sweet cake | A sort of French bread | *A small white bean | A large red fruit
exercise: In a French recipe you read «haricots verts». What does this mean? | Tinned tomatoes | Small white beans | Green peas | *Thin green beans
exercise: In which country are haricot beans called navy beans? | Ireland | Australia | *The US | The UK
test: Haricot is the French word for which food? | Soup | Cheese | *Bean | Bread
test: How do you say «haricot» correctly? | ha-REE-koh | *HA-ri-koh | HAR-ee-cot | HA-ri-koht
exam: Read this: «Add a tin of haricot beans to the soup.» What are haricot beans? | A tin opener | *Small white beans | A type of spoon | A soup pot
